{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20299",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.56,
      "end_seconds": 4.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.0,
      "end_seconds": 9.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.2,
      "end_seconds": 21.84,
      "duration_seconds": 10.64,
      "text": "Mainly pain in my right shoulder. There's a couple of other things, um, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.65,
      "end_seconds": 26.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.83,
      "end_seconds": 31.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "I've had it for about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.39,
      "end_seconds": 42.07,
      "duration_seconds": 9.68,
      "text": "alright, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.98,
      "end_seconds": 70.1,
      "duration_seconds": 26.12,
      "text": "It comes and goes. I'd call it mild. Only rest, and it's not much. Oh, and pain at night when I lie on it. That's been about the same, about three months. About pain at night when I lie on it, honestly, a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.66,
      "end_seconds": 74.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Any an ache down the upper arm as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.42,
      "end_seconds": 78.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Yes, for three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.84,
      "end_seconds": 84.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.98,
      "end_seconds": 88.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "it happens every other day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.62,
      "end_seconds": 96.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "So, did you get fever or neck pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.24,
      "end_seconds": 101.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "No, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.56,
      "end_seconds": 105.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Did you get fall or injury or swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.37,
      "end_seconds": 108.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "no, nothing to report there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.28,
      "end_seconds": 115.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.18,
      "end_seconds": 117.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.49,
      "end_seconds": 121.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.09,
      "end_seconds": 125.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "that's normal as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.35,
      "end_seconds": 148.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.71,
      "end_seconds": 154.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure for about ten years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.82,
      "end_seconds": 162.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.93,
      "text": "Alright, high blood pressure, that matches what I have here. A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.94,
      "end_seconds": 177.49,
      "duration_seconds": 13.55,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.04,
      "end_seconds": 183.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.15,
      "end_seconds": 187.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "No, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.97,
      "end_seconds": 192.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.81,
      "end_seconds": 200.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.75,
      "text": "Lisinopril, 10 milligrams, once a day. Diclofenac gel. I take it twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.11,
      "end_seconds": 220.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.43,
      "end_seconds": 236.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.86,
      "end_seconds": 258.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 117 over 70, heart rate 83."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.12,
      "end_seconds": 264.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.14,
      "end_seconds": 267.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "of course"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.18,
      "end_seconds": 269.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.5,
      "end_seconds": 290.1,
      "duration_seconds": 12.6,
      "text": "there is pain when you lift the arm out to the side between about sixty and one hundred and twenty degrees, and the grip strength is normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.17,
      "end_seconds": 292.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.16,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.37,
      "end_seconds": 299.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "You can relax now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.27,
      "end_seconds": 319.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a shoulder X-ray for shoulder pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 320.31,
      "end_seconds": 323.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "the earliest is Monday, 10 am"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.87,
      "end_seconds": 329.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Let's get an ultrasound of the shoulder, for shoulder pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 332.55,
      "end_seconds": 335.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "When would that take place?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.49,
      "end_seconds": 345.23,
      "duration_seconds": 8.74,
      "text": "keep the shoulder moving gently within comfort and avoid heavy overhead lifting. Please come and see me after the scan"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.83,
      "end_seconds": 347.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "I can manage that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.35,
      "end_seconds": 353.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "Can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 355.54,
      "end_seconds": 360.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "So, I come back after the scan. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.54,
      "end_seconds": 366.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.21,
      "end_seconds": 370.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}